      "text": "Since $n$ is 1 modulo 6, $n$ is either congruent to (mod) 1 or 7.\n\nThis means there are two possible scenarios for the answer:\n\nScenario 1: when $n+2010$ is 1 modulo 6\nScenario 2: when $n+2010$ is 7 modulo 6\n\nScenario 1 has a remainder of 1.\n\nScenario 2 has a remainder of 5.\n\nTherefore, the remainder is either 1 or 5.",
